{#
  The judicial lists' navigation: the shared pool, and the referrals this judge is holding.

  One partial rather than the same markup on two pages, because the pair is the point — a judge who claims a
  referral leaves the pool's list and must be able to get to the other one (`referrals-admin-6` decision 4). Both
  destinations are named here, so neither page can grow a link the other lacks.

  **Local to these two pages and deliberately not global chrome.** The `/judicial/**` middleware is the persona
  boundary, so this must not reach the caseworker's case list or the shared header: a caseworker who could see a
  judicial link would be offered a door the gate then shuts. That is also why it is not
  `govukServiceNavigation` — that component is the service's own chrome, renders its own
  `govuk-width-container`, and would sit inside the layout's, so using it here would mean nesting one width
  container in another to say something only two pages may say.

  A partial rather than a page: no `.ts` beside it, so `simple-router` ignores it while the directory stays on
  the Nunjucks search path. Import it directory-qualified — bare basenames are global and silently shadow each
  other.

  `aria-current="page"` on the current destination, which stays a link: it is where you are and also where the
  URL points, so there is nothing to take away. The state is announced by `aria-current`, printed as weight, and
  underlined by `app-judicial-nav__current` — three indicators, so it is carried neither by colour nor by
  boldness alone.
#}
{% macro judicialListNavigation(nav, current) %}
  <nav class="app-judicial-nav" aria-label="{{ nav.label }}">
    <ul class="app-judicial-nav__list">
      <li class="app-judicial-nav__item">
        <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state{% if current == 'pool' %} app-judicial-nav__current{% endif %}"
           href="/judicial/referrals"{% if current == 'pool' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ nav.pool }}</a>
      </li>
      <li class="app-judicial-nav__item">
        <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state{% if current == 'mine' %} app-judicial-nav__current{% endif %}"
           href="/judicial/referrals/mine"{% if current == 'mine' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ nav.mine }}</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
{% endmacro %}
